        "en" to GemDetails(
            "Astrophyllite is a complex potassium, iron, manganese and titanium silicate, a rare mineral of alkaline rocks. It crystallises in nepheline syenites and their pegmatites, igneous rocks very poor in silica and rich in sodium and potassium, in the last stages of crystallisation of these unusual magmas, together with aegirine, eudialyte, nepheline and feldspar. It forms golden-brown to brownish-black blades, grouped in rosettes or radiating stars within a pale matrix of feldspar and nepheline, hence its Greek name from “astron”, star, and “phyllon”, leaf.",
