            "Russia: the Kola Peninsula, Khibiny and Lovozero massifs, the main source of cabochons with golden stars on a white or grey ground. Norway: the Langesundsfjord (Larvik, Brevik), the historic locality of description. Canada: Mont Saint-Hilaire (Quebec), collector crystals. Also the United States (Colorado, St. Peters Dome; Montana), Greenland (Narsarsuk) and Guinea (Los Islands).",
            "A stone of self-discovery and hidden potential, said to let latent talents shine, help break free of old patterns and open one to new possibilities. It is associated with the solar plexus chakra and all the chakras, and the sign of Capricorn. Soft: avoid prolonged water and knocks; cleanse by smudging; recharge in moonlight."
